      "claim": "The regulation classifies individuals based on their status as drug users, those with drug convictions, or those in treatment, which is a non-suspect classification.",
      "evidence": "U.S. Supreme Court precedent (e.g., City of Cleburne v. Cleburne Living Center) establishes that classifications based on physical disability, mental disability, or other non-immutable/non-fundamental characteristics do not trigger heightened scrutiny. Drug use status is not a suspect or quasi-suspect class.",
