      "claim": "Because neither a suspect class nor a fundamental right is implicated, the applicable standard of review is the rational basis test.",
      "evidence": "Standard Equal Protection doctrine dictates that if the classification is non-suspect and the right is non-fundamental, the government action is valid if it is rationally related to a legitimate state interest.",
